                "one syllable, so the beat cannot fall elsewhere"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "No choice to correct.",
                "incorrect": "One syllable -- there is nowhere else the stress could go."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Why does vi carry no accent? (One syllable — the beat has nowhere else to fall.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And what is \"I saw\"? (Vi.) Next: a second verb that does the same thing, and it is one you have never met."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ES-C65-di",
      "sequence": 2512,
      "title": "di — the verb that changed families in the past",
      "headword": "di",
      "romanization": "di",
      "gloss": "I gave — an -ar verb that takes -er endings in the past, and goes as bare as vi",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:42cebc6bfe54740f",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Vi, viste, vio — bare, because one syllable has nowhere else to put the beat."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A second verb does the same, and it is one you have never met."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: dar, which behaves like an -er verb",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Dar means to give. It is an -ar verb — and in the preterite it flatly refuses to behave like one:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dar becomes di, diste, dio, dimos, disteis, dieron."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Those are the -er endings, on an -ar verb, with the same one-syllable forms going bare. Ver does the same in the plural: vimos, visteis, vieron."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two verbs, one shared oddity, and now the last two named irregulars of the preterite are yours."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "di, diste, dio",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *di*, *diste*, *dio*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "vi, viste, vio, then di, diste, dio",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *vi*, *viste*, *vio*, then *di*, *diste*, *dio*]"
            },
